# Bitloop project and skill routing

Actions: use the existing Bitloop lifecycle, CMake integration, drawing, camera/input and diagnostic facilities. Workers start with [bitloop-development](../../.agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md), then load only references relevant to their task. Planning/review receives this catalogue, not the linked manuals.

Prerequisites: follow [Substrate instructions](../../AGENTS.md), identify the active target/build and inspect its Bitloop headers for exact APIs. Hints describe framework facilities, not implemented Substrate features or successful checks. Keep simulation ownership in this project; changes to framework/other owners require the applicable authorization.

Evidence: compile the smallest relevant target for wiring; use semantic checks for physics, snapshots for visual claims and measured benchmarks for performance. Record capability IDs, actual commands/configuration, observations, limits and retained evidence paths in the MindGraph task result's supported fields.

## Details

Build routing: [configure/build/run](../../.agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/configure-build-run.md), [CMake](../../.agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/build-cmake.md). Use Codex-owned presets/directories; preserve user build state. A missing matching package is a reported prerequisite, not permission to update dependencies.

Implementation routing: [lifecycle](../../.agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/scene-lifecycle.md), [ImGui](../../.agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/imgui-ui.md), [drawing](../../.agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/drawing.md), [threading](../../.agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/threading.md), [performance](../../.agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/performance.md). Read the skill's full routing index only when needed; do not copy it into each plan task.

These project-authored hints complement the managed skill; refresh them when local capabilities change. MindGraph fingerprints hints and their direct local links, but does not discover installed framework versions or certify runtime support.
